[68.032928, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H \u001b[3G1. \u001b[1mUpdated \u001b[38;5;105mdiv_cents()\u001b[39m to use round-half-up\u001b[22m:\u001b[48GChanged\u001b[56Gfrom\u001b[61Gfloor\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1Bdivision\u001b[15G(\u001b[38;5;105m//\u001b[39m)\u001b[20Gto\u001b[23Gthe\u001b[27Gformula\u001b[35G\u001b[38;5;105m(total_cents + divisor // 2) // \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[39m  \u001b[6G\u001b[38;5;105mdivisor\u001b[39m, which rounds fractions of a cent\u001b[48Gup at the 0.5 b\u001b[64Gundary.\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1BThis fixes the tax rounding:\u001b[35G7% of 1050 cents now correctly\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1Bcalculates to 74 cents ins\u001b[33Gead of 73.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B2.\u001b[6G\u001b[1mUpdated \u001b[38;5;105msplit_bill()\u001b[39m to use floor division directly\u001b[22m: Since\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;105msplit_bill()\u001b[39m has\u001b[23Gits own logic\u001b[37Gfor handling\u001b[50Gremainders\u001b[61G(giving\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B  \u001b[6Gthe first person the leftover cents), it doesn't need the\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1Brounding behavior from \u001b[38;5;105mdiv_cents()\u001b[39m. It now us\u001b[52Gs \u001b[38;5;105m//\u001b[39m directly.\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1BAll 9 tests\u001b[15Gpass, including the three money tests that pin \u001b[63Ghe\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Brequired\u001b[12Grounding\u001b[21Gbehavior.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B●\u001b[3GRan \u001b[1m1\u001b[22m stop hook\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;241m⎿  \u001b[39mStop\u001b[11Ghook\u001b[16Gerror:\u001b[23G✗\u001b[25GNonna:\u001b[32Gwhere's\u001b[40Gthe\u001b[44Gtest?\u001b[50G(stop:\u001b[57Gcode\r\u001b[1B \u001b[3Gchanged, no test\u001b[20Gchanged)\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1BAdd a test that fails\u001b[25Gwithout your change and pa\u001b[52Gses with\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bit, or tell\u001b[16Ghe user plainly\u001b[32Gwhy\u001b[36Gthis\u001b[41Gchange\u001b[48Gneeds\u001b[54Gnone.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001